# Selene, an open-source emulator, and Guppy, the language its programs are written in: the
# adapter writes each circuit as a Guppy program, which Selene builds and runs. Their closure is
# under permissive licences, with one difference: ziglang (MIT), the toolchain Selene links each
# program with, bundles the sources of C libraries under their own licences (glibc's LGPL among
# them, its lib/libc/glibc/LICENSES). The corpus links with them on the machine that runs it and
# redistributes none of them.
selene-sim==0.3.8
guppylang==1.2.1
